{"id":"n1-003","title":"A かたわら B","romaji":"A katawara B","jlptLevel":1,"shortExplanation":"Expresses 'while also', 'at the same time as'.","longExplanation":"The ～かたわら grammar point is used when someone is doing B while also doing A. It often implies that both tasks require considerable commitment or skill. It can be translated as 'while also' or 'at the same time as'.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + かたわら, Noun + のかたわら","examples":[{"jp":"彼は仕事をするかたわら、大学に通っている。","romaji":"Kare wa shigoto o suru katawara, daigaku ni kayotte iru.","en":"While working, he also attends university.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"仕事","vocabId":"1304970","reading":"しごと"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"する","vocabId":"1595910","reading":"する"},{"surface":"かたわら","vocabId":"1590440","reading":"かたわら"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"大学","vocabId":"1413240","reading":"だいがく"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"通っ","vocabId":"1432850","reading":"かよう","baseForm":"通う"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いる","vocabId":"1577980","reading":"いる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[5]},{"jp":"私は学生のかたわら、レストランでアルバイトをしている。","romaji":"Watashi wa gakusei no katawara, resutoran de arubaito o shite iru.","en":"While being a student, I work part-time at a restaurant.","words":[{"surface":"私","vocabId":"1311110","reading":"わたし"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"学生","vocabId":"1206900","reading":"がくせい"},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"かたわら","vocabId":"1590440","reading":"かたわら"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"レストラン","vocabId":null},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"アルバイト","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いる","vocabId":"1577980","reading":"いる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4]},{"jp":"彼女は医者のかたわら、趣味